<title>RUSSIA: Russian Sberbank cuts credit rates for households.</title>
<headline>Russian Sberbank cuts credit rates for households.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sberbank, Russia's biggest bank, cut its credit rates for households from June 23, 1997, to 27 percent from 29 percent, the bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Sberbank spokesman said the Moscow branch of Sberbank set a 19 percent rate for credits to households in hard currency from June 23.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
